---
/**
 * Privacy for a small business website that collects almost nothing.
 *
 * Written for what these sites actually do rather than adapted from a SaaS
 * policy: there are no accounts, no tracking cookies and no advertising
 * network, and saying so plainly is both more honest and more useful than
 * three thousand words hedging about "partners".
 *
 * If a client adds analytics, a booking system or a shop, this page has to
 * change with it. A policy describing a site that no longer exists is worse
 * than none.
 */
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { site } from '../lib/site';

const updated = new Date().toISOString().slice(0, 10);
const c = site.contact;
---

<Base title="Privacy" path="/privacy" description={`How ${site.name} handles your information.`}>
  <section>
    <div class="wrap prose">
      <h1>Privacy</h1>
      <p class="lede">Last updated {updated}.</p>

      <h2>The short version</h2>
      <p>
        This website does not have accounts, does not show advertising, and does not
        use tracking cookies. If you do not contact us, we do not learn anything
        about you beyond what any web server records in order to serve a page.
      </p>

      <h2>What the server records</h2>
      <p>
        Our host keeps ordinary web server logs — the page requested, the time, the
        browser, and an IP address — which are used to keep the site working and
        secure. They are not used to build a profile of you and are not sold.
      </p>

      <h2>If you contact us</h2>
      <p>
        When you call, email or write to us, we keep what you sent so that we can
        answer it and so that we have a record of what was agreed. We do not add
        you to a mailing list because you got in touch.
      </p>

      <h2>Cookies</h2>
      <p>
        This site sets no cookies of its own. If that changes — a booking system or
        a shop would change it — this page will say so before it does.
      </p>

      <h2>Other people's services</h2>
      <p>
        Pages that embed something from elsewhere, such as a map or a video, let
        that company see that your browser loaded it. Their handling of that is
        theirs, not ours.
      </p>

      <h2>Your choices</h2>
      <p>
        You can ask what we hold about you, ask for it to be corrected, or ask for
        it to be deleted, and we will do it. Ask using any of the contact details
        on this site{c.email ? ` — ${c.email} reaches us` : ''}.
      </p>

      <h2>Children</h2>
      <p>
        This site is not directed at children and we do not knowingly collect
        information from them.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes</h2>
      <p>
        If this policy changes, the date at the top changes with it.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .prose { max-width: var(--measure); }
  .prose h2 { font-size: 1.2rem; margin-top: 2rem; }
</style>
